# TypeScript + Next.js 15 / React 19 Production Rules
- Strict TypeScript (`strict: true`, zero `any` on public boundaries, explicit return types on exported functions).
- Prefer React Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only for stateful/interactive leaf components.
- Validate all Route Handler / Server Action payloads with Zod before touching DB or external APIs.
- Handle loading, empty, and error states explicitly; never ignore rejected Promises.
- Avoid N+1 queries; batch relational reads and enforce tenant/user authorization at the data access boundary.
